AGPL section 13 — remote network interaction

Velnox is network-accessed software. Section 13 of the AGPLv3 requires that
users interacting with a modified version over a network be offered the
Corresponding Source of that version.

Velnox satisfies this obligation in the product itself: the Settings > About
screen and the API endpoint GET /api/v1/system/source display the version, the
build commit, and a link from which the Corresponding Source of the running
build can be obtained. Operators running a modified build MUST keep that link
pointing at their own modified source. Removing the notice does not remove the
obligation.

